course: dictionary
lesson: 4037
title: Gear: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Gear can mean kit, a toothed wheel in a machine, a setting on a bike, or getting ready. «Every sport has rules and safety gear» is about kit. «Low gears give a strong push to start and climb hills» is about a bike setting.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «The gears on a bike are toothed wheels joined by the chain» tells you that gears are wheels with teeth. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Your meaning must match the whole sentence, not just one word. If you think gear means clothes, try it in «a small gear at the back makes the wheel turn faster». It does not fit, so this gear must be a wheel.
fact: Gear can mean equipment or kit, such as «safety gear» like helmets and knee pads.
fact: A gear is a wheel with teeth around the edge that turns another toothed wheel.
fact: On a bike, a low gear makes going uphill easier, and «high gears let the wheels turn fast».
fact: A small gear turning a big gear makes it turn slower but with more force.
fact: «Gear up» means get ready.
exercise: «Every sport has rules and safety gear: shin pads in soccer.» What does gear mean here? | * Equipment or kit you wear for an activity | A toothed wheel in a machine | A slow setting on a bike | Getting ready to play
exercise: «The gears on a bike are toothed wheels joined by the chain.» In this sentence, what are gears? | Clothes for cycling | Pedals that you push with your feet | Brakes that stop the bike | * Wheels with teeth that pass turning from one part to another
exercise: Mum says, «Let's gear up for the match.» What does gear up mean? | Slow down | * Get ready | Take off your kit | Change the wheels
test: «Low gears give a strong push to start and climb hills.» What does a low gear help with? | Going fast on flat ground | Stopping the bike quickly | * Starting and climbing hills | Turning off the lights
test: «A small gear at the back makes the wheel turn faster.» Which gear makes the wheel turn faster? | Neither one | A gear with no teeth | * A small gear | A big gear
exam: Ella says gear only ever means clothes. Why is she wrong? | Gear means to sleep | Gear only means a hill | Gear only means clothes and kit | * Gear also means a toothed wheel in a machine, and a setting on a bike
